description:
Static map of a Python repository. New exports are versioned documents (schema_version 1.0.0). Maps written before that version are a JSON array of the same file records and remain valid for readers.

Paths are repository-relative and use forward slashes. The src/ directory prefix is kept in paths and ids; it is stripped only when deriving a Python module name for import resolution.

Directories named .git, .venv, __pycache__, and node_modules are skipped. Files that fail to parse are omitted.

Stable ids identify a file, class, method, or function inside one map. They stay the same across runs when the relative path and definition name stay the same. A line number is appended only when a file has more than one top-level definition with that name, and is always included for definitions nested inside a function. Those line-qualified ids change if the definition moves to a different line.

Id grammar:
- file:{path}
- class:{path}:{name} or class:{path}:{name}:{line}
- method:{path}:{class}:{name} or method:{path}:{class}:{name}:{line}
- function:{path}:{name} or function:{path}:{name}:{line}

Nested classes and functions always use the line-qualified form. Nested methods use method:{path}:{class}:{name}:{line}.
